WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.376
Ghostwriter. He’s back.

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.920
In three, two, one.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.097
Whoa.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.642
I thought moving here and starting
a new school would be hard.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.855
But I found friends I
never imagined I’d find.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:22.647
Chevon.

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:23.481
Curtis.

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:24.274
And Donna.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:25.942
It changed everything.

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:29.696
There’s a logical explanation.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.572
It’s a ghost.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:33.241
I think the ghost can only
communicate with written words.

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:34.534
The ghost writer?

00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:36.619
Do you have the time?

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:38.705
There’s a talking rabbit that
nobody can see but us.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:41.541
I think the rabbit from
this book has escaped.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.500
Who let him out?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.210
The ghost who’s been
sending us messages.

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:45.462
What is this?

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:46.504
What are you doing?

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:47.589
Horrifying.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.300
What if your grandma’s ghostwriter?

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.136
Grandpa said even though grandma’s
gone she’ll always be with us.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.637
Like a ghost.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:57.015
And they only hang around when
they have unfinished business.

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:58.141
Let’s do this.

00:00:58.141 --> 00:00:59.684
Your grandma had this old letter.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:00.810
Secret letter?

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:01.936
It must’ve been important.

00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:03.271
We need to find that letter.

00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:05.648
Ghostwriter let the characters out of the book.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:08.818
Grandma wouldn’t have sent them here
unless they were important to the mystery.

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:10.153
Grandma’s letter.

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:13.531
Who’s “S”?

00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:15.158
The mystery is nowhere
close to being solved.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.203
I’m pretty good at solving mysteries.

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.829
Sparkles, they’re memories

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:20.997
left behind by other people.

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:24.667
That’s my grandma.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.753
There was a weird guy that gave
a check to grandma and it was

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.129
inside the Mason Briggs book.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.258
That’s grandma’s letter.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.802
So that person is “S.”

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:34.969
But who is it?

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.346
We need to find him.

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.599
That lady that used to work here…

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.308
My grandma.

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:43.645
She was sure that this
bookstore was haunted.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.775
If my grandma’s not Ghostwriter, then
who have we been talking to all this time?

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.361
Ghostwriter wasn’t releasing your paintings.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.613
The character in this case
would be the paint brush.

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:55.949
Cobalt Mask.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.616
The painting.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:00.161
There’s no author. That’s a first.

00:02:01.037 --> 00:02:01.871
Frank is from a poem.

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:03.289
He’s a spy.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.251
He’s also from a bunch of
Mason Briggs books.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.378
Mason Briggs wrote detective fiction.

00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:10.421
At which point he drops off the map.

00:02:10.421 --> 00:02:12.423
The Cobalt Mask never came out.

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:14.592
And he has an unpublished manuscript.

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:17.303
Mason Briggs has to be involved 
in the mystery somehow.

00:02:18.888 --> 00:02:20.140
Sherlock Holmes.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.099
Doctor Watson?

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.475
We need help solving a case.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.518
Let the facts lead you.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.229
Mason Briggs is a pseudonym.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:30.567
This photo allowed us to 
find the real Mason Briggs.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.736
This technology is fantastic.

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:35.405
No kidding, Sherlock.

00:02:36.364 --> 00:02:38.783
If we find this view, we find the manuscript.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:40.869
Look!

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.162
Nice view.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.621
Check this out.

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.874
We’re so close to finishing the mystery.

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:49.586
Time travel.

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:50.628
This is incredible.

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.091
Pirates.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.176
Dinosaurs!

00:02:57.218 --> 00:02:58.428
Did that rat just drive that car?

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.346
This is gonna be interesting.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.309
Ghostwriter’s been preparing 
us for this moment.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:07.312
We’re running out of time.

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:12.775
We went in to the book.

00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:14.194
We became book characters?

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.695
Stylin’.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.534
This food is so amazing.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.077
Didn’t you eat breakfast this morning?

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:25.413
Yeah, but book eggs taste way better.

